  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    A deep-carved chamber three fathoms beneath the Wane☽ Oncea collapse-tunnels, ☽'dwell Teneanemus~ — universally called **the Scar-Keep** by locals, who avoid the formal name — was created during the Frozen Peace as a recovery site for Nightshelf blood-rites believed destroyed during the Orca Incursion. It now serves as contested ground between Qingfu'spire, the Aurora-aligned surface council, and ☽'shadow Covens' Order, the diminished Nightshelf shadow parliament. Neither faction will formally claim jurisdiction. Neither will relinquish it.
    
    ## Physical Description
    
    The chamber accommodates roughly forty penguins and is accessible through a single entrance marked by a deliberately unmarked stone — an open secret. Its walls bear the Grend-thung-blood sigils, not freshly carved but *recovered*: chiseled back into visibility after generations of deliberate plaster and ice-seal. These sigils exhibit resonance geometry consistent with aurora-crystal lattice structures, a correspondence noted independently by practitioners of both disciplines and not yet adequately explained.
    
    Fire-braziers maintain a steady 15.7 degrees — anomalous for this depth. The Scared~ Shroud, a fire-core tome bound in volcanic glass and ancestor bone containing the recovered Grend Blood-Rites, rests in an obsidian alcove at the chamber's center. Names are carved into the living ice above it in both Qingfu'spire formal script and ☽'shadow Covens' rougher hand. Beneath these, in nearly invisible charcoal scratches, someone wrote *Kess was here*. The identity of Kess is unrecorded.
    
    ## Significance and Contested Use
    
    The chamber's practical importance was demonstrated when Lianhinglou, a Nightshelf beacon-keeper, entered ☽'dwell Teneanemus~ during a resource crisis and recovered techniques combining aurora-light with deep-pressure methods — the Shell Hatch practice that allowed Founder Mingmeyang to map krill blooms. The cost was Lianhinglou's memories. The sigils' corruption-link to Pod-bond Annihilation, the cataclysmic spell cast during the Shelf Crushing Offense, remains attested but poorly documented.
    
    Locals leave offerings of rendered fat beside the Shroud. The last two caretakers who neglected this practice reportedly lost their sight within a season. I note this without endorsement. The jurisdictional deadlock between Qingfu'spire and ☽'shadow Covens' Order predates the end of the Orca Incursion, leaving the chamber effectively unmonitored — which, given what has been retrieved from it, should concern someone.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771591131515_0", anchor: "predates the end of the Orca Incursion, leaving the chamber effectively unmonitored", text: "Created during the Frozen Peace, I wrote in the overview — which postdates the Orca Incursion. Then down here I claim the jurisdictional deadlock predates its end. Both cannot be true of the chamber. They can be true of the *site*: the raw tunnel space was contested before anyone carved it into a recovery chamber. The Wane☽ Oncea collapse-strata preserve territorial markings from at least three factions at this depth, none of them Qingfu'spire, who did not yet exist. I conflated the tunnel with the institution built inside it. Sloppy. The kind of error I would have caught in someone else's work immediately and in my own only after it was set in ice.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771591131515_1", anchor: "Fire-braziers maintain a steady 15.7 degrees", text: "\"Effectively unmonitored,\" I wrote four sentences later, about a chamber where someone maintains temperature to a tenth of a degree. That is not unmonitored. That is monitored by someone who declines to file paperwork.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771591131515_2", anchor: "The last two caretakers who neglected this practice reportedly lost their sight within a season", text: "Reportedly. By whom? I traced this to a single ☽'shadow Covens' source who also claimed the Shroud hums during the Long Dark. The humming I can corroborate — acoustic resonance from fire-core tomes at low ambient temperature is well-documented. The blindness I cannot. Two is not a pattern. It is a coincidence with good narrative timing.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
